@startuml 02-data-flow
' End-to-end data flow with every destination an event can reach.
' Render: make diagrams

title Data Flow — every event reaches exactly one destination

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam roundCorner 6
skinparam ArrowColor #445566
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #445566
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

rectangle "<b>NDJSON files</b> + manifest\none line per event; the manifest\nrecords the verdict each event <i>must</i> receive" as FILES #FFF8E7

rectangle "<b>@RAW.TRADE_LANDING</b>\ninternal stage" as STAGE #EAFBEF

rectangle "<b>RAW.TRADE_EVENT</b>\nVARIANT payload, insert-only\n14-day Time Travel" as RAW #EAFBEF
rectangle "<b>RAW.COPY_ERROR</b>\nraw line retained\n<i>never reached the rule engine</i>" as CERR #FBEAEA

rectangle "<b>RAW.TRADE_EVENT_STREAM</b>\nAPPEND_ONLY, transactional offset" as STREAM #EAFBEF
rectangle "<b>RAW.TRADE_EVENT_QUEUE</b>\n<b>the contract dbt reads</b>" as QUEUE #D9F2E3

rectangle "<b>stg_trade_event</b>\nview — rename only, no logic" as STG #EAF3FB
rectangle "<b>int_trade_event_typed</b>\ntry_to_* casts\n+ cast_failure_count" as TYPED #EAF3FB

rectangle "<b>int_trade_event_adjudicated</b>\n1. FIELD rules\n2. version arbitration <i>(field-valid only)</i>\n3. STATE rules\n4. verdict" as ADJ #C9DEF5

rectangle "<b>CORE.FCT_TRADE</b>\ngolden record\ncurrent version + lifecycle" as FCT #D9F2E3
rectangle "<b>CORE.FCT_TRADE_VERSION</b>\nversion ledger\nevery accepted version" as FCTV #D9F2E3
rectangle "<b>AUDIT.FCT_TRADE_REJECTED</b>\n+ raw_payload as it arrived" as REJ #FBEAEA
rectangle "<b>AUDIT.TRADE_RULE_RESULT</b>\none row per (event, rule)\nincluding WARN on accepted trades" as RR #FBF3EA

rectangle "<b>SNAPSHOTS.SNP_TRADE</b>\nSCD2 — captures transitions\nthat have <i>no event</i> (expiry)" as SNAP #F3EAFB
rectangle "<b>REPORTING.*</b>\naggregates +\nDQ scorecard" as REP #F3EAFB

FILES --> STAGE : PUT
STAGE --> RAW : COPY INTO\nON_ERROR = CONTINUE
STAGE --> CERR : line could not be parsed
RAW --> STREAM : stream captures the delta
STREAM --> QUEUE : SP_DRAIN — <b>one transaction</b>\ninsert + batch record + offset advance
QUEUE --> STG
STG --> TYPED
TYPED --> ADJ

ADJ --> FCT : ACCEPTED
ADJ --> FCTV : ACCEPTED
ADJ --> REJ : REJECTED\nor SUPERSEDED
ADJ --> RR : every rule that fired

FCT --> SNAP
FCT --> REP
REJ --> REP

note right of ADJ
  <b>Why FIELD precedes STATE</b>

  Arbitration uses only field-valid events.
  A malformed v5 must not set the high-water
  mark, or a valid v3 would then be rejected
  as stale on the authority of an event we
  already refused.
end note

note bottom of REJ
  <b>assert_no_event_is_silently_dropped</b>
  Every event entering the queue must reach
  exactly one of FCT_TRADE, FCT_TRADE_REJECTED
  (rejected), or FCT_TRADE_REJECTED (superseded).
  A violation is silent data loss — P1.
end note

note left of QUEUE
  The ingestion mechanism can be replaced
  (Snowpipe Streaming, Kafka connector,
  external table) without any dbt model
  changing. This is what makes scaling
  to 10,000x tractable.
end note

note right of CERR
  ON_ERROR = CONTINUE means one bad line
  cannot block a file — and is exactly what
  makes loss invisible. Hence COPY_ERROR
  and vw_copy_history's PARTIAL_LOAD.
end note

@enduml
